      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auburn%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "On April 10, 1778, parts of Worcester, Sutton, Leicester and Oxford were incorporated as the Town of Ward in honor of General Artemas Ward.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auburn%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1837 the town changed its name from Ward to Auburn, a name that still echoes today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.auburnma.gov/381/About-Our-Town",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Robert Goddard launched the first liquid‑fueled rocket from Pakachoag Hill on March 16, 1926, a milestone in spaceflight history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auburn%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A replica of Goddard’s prototype now sits proudly in Auburn High School, a reminder of the town’s pioneering spirit.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auburn%2C_Massachusetts",
